SOURCE_TITLE=Small generators of the ideal class group
AUTHORS=Karim Belabas; Francisco Diaz y Diaz; Eduardo Friedman
PUBLICATION=Mathematics of Computation 77 (2008), 1185-1197
DOI=10.1090/S0025-5718-07-02003-0
SOURCE_URL=https://www.math.u-bordeaux.fr/~kbelabas/research/OnBach.pdf
SOURCE_PDF_SHA256=e619d0f0c52bfddd0316e354d72c1b3b7946d85a1cdcbad05aac990cf911fc78
SOURCE_LOCATION=Section 5; Theorem 5.1; Corollary 5.2; equations (23)-(24)

AUDITED_STATEMENT:
For every T>1, the strict inequality in Corollary 5.2 implies that the
classes of all prime ideals of K with norm strictly less than T generate the
full ideal class group.  Section 5 explicitly drops GRH.  The full sums in
this scan include every prime ideal and every power with N(P)^m<T; the
degree-one sums are separately labelled sufficient lower sub-sums.

FIELD_LEDGER:
K=Q(alpha), alpha^31=2.  Since 2^30 mod 31^2 is 187, not 1, the standard
pure-prime-degree index criterion gives O_K=Z[alpha].  Thus n=31, r1=1, and
|Delta_K|=2^30*31^31.  The exact binomial splitting law is independently
checked by direct finite-field factorization whenever a residue degree above
one can enter the largest strict cutoff.

SCAN_LEDGER:
The only tested cutoffs are 40000000, 80000000, 160000000, and 320000000.
Prime enumeration is segmented and exact.  RealBall precision is 256 bits.
No principal-ideal witnesses, BNF, class group, regulator, or unit group are
constructed.
